import json,sys,statistics,math,html
from pathlib import Path
root=Path(sys.argv[1]);rows=[json.loads(l) for l in (root/'games.jsonl').read_text().splitlines()];labels=['draw3-paid','draw2-paid','draw3-free','draw2-free']
def avg(a):return statistics.mean(a) if a else None
def fmt(x):return '—' if x is None else f'{x:.1f}'
def ci(a):
 if len(a)<2:return None
 m=avg(a);e=1.96*statistics.stdev(a)/math.sqrt(len(a));return [m-e,m+e]
def summary(a):
 valid=[x for x in a if x['status']!='failed'];fin=[x for x in valid if x['endReason']=='finish'];rounds={}
 for x in valid:
  for k,v in x['byRound'].items():
   out=rounds.setdefault(k,{name:0 for name in v})
   for name,val in v.items():out[name]+=val
 return {'n':len(a),'finish':len(fin),'exhaustion':sum(x['endReason']=='deckExhausted' for x in valid),'censored':sum(x['status']=='censored' for x in valid),'failed':len(a)-len(valid),'gap':avg([x['range'] for x in fin]),'gapCI':ci([x['range'] for x in fin]),'third':avg([x['thirdLag'] for x in fin]),'actions':avg([x['actions'] for x in valid]),'p90Actions':sorted(x['actions'] for x in valid)[math.ceil(.9*len(valid))-1] if valid else None,'hands':avg([sum(x['hands']) for x in fin]),'calls':avg([x['calls'] for x in valid]),'nonCalls':avg([x['nonCalls'] for x in valid]),'movement':{k:avg([x['winMovement'][k] for x in fin]) for k in ['ownCall','otherCall','valueAction','changeFounder','raiseMoney']},'rounds':rounds}
m={k:summary([x for x in rows if x['config']==k]) for k in labels};byPlayer={k:{str(n):summary([x for x in rows if x['config']==k and x['players']==n]) for n in [2,3,4]} for k in labels};(root/'metrics.json').write_text(json.dumps({'groups':m,'byPlayer':byPlayer},indent=2));print(json.dumps({k:{j:v for j,v in a.items() if j!='rounds'} for k,a in m.items()},indent=2))
if not (root/'reviews.json').exists():sys.exit()
reviews=json.loads((root/'reviews.json').read_text());manifest=json.loads((root/'manifest.json').read_text());idx=json.loads((root/'sample-index.json').read_text())
def table(head,body):return '<table><tr>'+''.join('<th>'+str(x)+'</th>' for x in head)+'</tr>'+''.join('<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+str(x)+'</td>' for x in r)+'</tr>' for r in body)+'</table>'
def access(a,k):
 r=a['rounds'].get(str(k),{});return fmt(100*(1-r.get('uniqueAccess',0)/r['unique']))+'%' if r.get('unique',0) else '—'
parts=['''<!doctype html><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Draw two and free actions — v134 experiment</title><style>body{max-width:1050px;margin:auto;padding:32px;font:17px/1.55 system-ui;background:#f7f4ed;color:#252b28}h1{font-size:36px;line-height:1.15}h2{font-size:23px}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:14px}th,td{text-align:left;padding:10px;border-bottom:1px solid #ccc}th{background:#e4e9e1}a{color:#16634e}details{padding:16px;border:1px solid #c9cfc4;border-radius:10px;margin:24px 0}summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:650}code{font-size:12px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}</style><p>VESTS · v134 RESEARCH CONFIGURATIONS · 8 November 2026</p><h1>Individual-hand scarcity is real.</h1><p>With five starting cards and nine copies per company, a player's chance of holding <b>no card for a specified company is 38.6%</b>: C(45,5)/C(54,5). The expected count is only 5/6 of a card. Knowing somebody at the table has one is not the same as being able to fund it. Bots never see opponents' deal-flow hands.</p><p>The previous report's table-wide supply and all-game averages did not establish whether scarcity constrains the acting player early. This experiment measures that directly, and tests drawing two versus three alongside removing the card cost from non-funding actions.</p><h2>Four-way comparison</h2><p>All configurations use nine cards/company, five starting cards and the same bots. “Free” means capital, founder and value actions spend no deal-flow card; each still takes the player's one turn. Fundraising always consumes a matching card. No other rules change.</p>''']
parts.append(table(['Configuration','Reached 24','Exhausted / censored','First–last*','First–third*','Actions'],[[k,f"{a['finish']}/{a['n']}",f"{a['exhaustion']} / {a['censored']}",fmt(a['gap']),fmt(a['third']),fmt(a['actions'])] for k,a in m.items()]))
parts.append('<p><b>Both changes together reached 24 in 120/120 games, but the mean first–last gap remained 22.2 spaces.</b> Drawing two increases individual-hand scarcity; making support actions card-free preserves funding opportunities and removed exhaustion in this sample. Neither change established a tight race. The initial 38.6% calculation describes a specified company before play; the measured table below follows the changing leader.</p>')
parts.append('<p>*Spread only among games reaching 24. Actions include any censored games up to the diagnostic cutoff; they are not human minutes. These are 120 games/configuration: 20 seeds × 2 lineups × 3 player counts. Small differences are not proof of a balance improvement.</p>')
parts.append('<h2>Does the acting player lack the leader’s card?</h2><p>Percentage of turns with <b>no matching card for the unique current leader</b>, restricted to turns where a unique leader exists. No opponent-hand knowledge is used. Later rounds contain only games still running, so changes across rounds also reflect survival of longer games.</p>')
parts.append(table(['Configuration','Round 1','Round 2','Round 3','Round 4','Round 5','Cards left in hands at finish*'],[[k,*[access(a,r) for r in range(1,6)],fmt(a['hands'])] for k,a in m.items()]))
parts.append('''<p>Drawing two reduces incoming options. Removing discards preserves outgoing options. Both can happen at once: until the deck empties, a non-funding turn with two draws increases the hand by two cards; a funding turn increases it by one. There is still no hand cap. Preserving a laggard card does not oblige anyone to invest in that company.</p><h2>What the “4.5 spaces” actually meant</h2><p>That older figure combined <b>all actions except the winner's own matching-card fundraisings</b>. It included value cards played on the winner itself. Calling it “movement during other companies' actions” was inaccurate.</p><p>A concrete previous example is <a href="../../dice-finite-v133/scarcity-02/samples/5004.json">sample 5004</a>: company 1 gets four +1 Gill activations during fundraisings in other companies (events 97, 111, 139, 176), plus a net +4 from Sweat played on company 1 (events 229–235: −2 then a six-space reveal). Those are eight outside-own-fundraising spaces, but only four come from other-company fundraising.</p><p>New winner-movement accounting separates the initiating actions below. All figures are net spaces after setup, among games reaching 24. Founder reactions remain attributed to the action that triggered them; own-call movement is not pure dice movement.</p>''')
parts.append(table(['Configuration','Own matching calls','Other-company matching calls','Value actions','Hire / capital actions'],[[k,fmt(a['movement']['ownCall']),fmt(a['movement']['otherCall']),fmt(a['movement']['valueAction']),fmt((a['movement']['changeFounder'] or 0)+(a['movement']['raiseMoney'] or 0))] for k,a in m.items()]))
parts.append('<details><summary>Player counts, uncertainty and action usage</summary>')
parts.append(table(['Config','Players','Finish','Gap (95% interval)*','Third*','Actions / p90','Funding / other actions'],[[k,n,f"{a['finish']}/{a['n']}",fmt(a['gap'])+' ('+'–'.join(map(fmt,a['gapCI'] or []))+')',fmt(a['third']),fmt(a['actions'])+' / '+str(a['p90Actions']),fmt(a['calls'])+' / '+fmt(a['nonCalls'])] for k,group in byPlayer.items() for n,a in group.items()]))
parts.append('<p>Observed finish rates are 115/120 for each paid configuration and 120/120 for each free configuration; approximate Wilson 95% intervals are 90.6–98.2% and 96.9–100%, respectively. Zero observed failures does not mean zero true failure probability. Gap intervals are approximate game-level intervals conditional on finishing and these policies. Access is a descriptive turn ratio; it is not treated as independent Bernoulli observations across turns. Provisional goals are ≥95% games reaching 24, mean first–last ≤16 and first–third ≤8 among finishes. Both versions of the scarcity metric (any tied leader and a deterministic single leader) and their denominators remain in metrics.json; the visible table uses unique leaders only.</p></details><details><summary>Ten complete replay reviews</summary><p>Fixed seeds, not selected outcomes. E/D indexes are zero-based event/decision indexes. Nine-copy supply throughout; v134 experimental engine. Exhaustion settlements remain reviewed but are not counted as reaches-24 successes.</p>')
for seed,title,arc,choice in reviews:parts.append(f'<h3><a href="samples/{seed}.json">{seed}</a> — {html.escape(title)}</h3><p>{html.escape(arc)}</p><p>{html.escape(choice)}</p>')
parts.append('</details><details><summary>Reproduce, inspect and verify</summary>')
parts.append(f'<p>{len(rows)} aggregate attempts; '+str(sum(x['status']=='complete' for x in rows))+' complete; '+str(sum(x['status']=='censored' for x in rows))+' censored; '+str(sum(x['status']=='failed' for x in rows))+' failed. Ten complete samples, '+str(len(idx))+' sample attempts. Source SHA-256: <code>'+manifest['source']+'</code>.</p>')
parts.append('''<p><a href="manifest.json">Protocol</a> · <a href="games.jsonl">Raw data</a> · <a href="metrics.json">Metrics and denominators</a> · <a href="sample-index.json">Sample selection</a> · <a href="reviews.json">Reviews</a> · <a href="runtime.json">Runtime</a> · <a href="source/scripts/flow-economy-study.js">Frozen runner</a></p><p><code>node scripts/flow-economy-study.js docs/dice-flow-v134/NEW-RUN 20 6001</code><br><code>python3 scripts/flow-economy-report.py docs/dice-flow-v134/NEW-RUN</code></p><p>Reproduce from source/ to use the exact frozen engine. Report generation also requires the written reviews.json. Seeds 6001–6020, balanced self-play and mixed balanced/growth/saver/random rotated by seed. Random samples enumerated legal action candidates and affordable integer bid amounts. Exact interactive dice forecasts retained; empty-hand guard is the only bot-code adaptation. Source versions and report data are immutable per run. Matched seeds share setup, not all later random outcomes. Limits: 150 completed actions or 2000 commands, explicitly censored rather than settled. Live v133 and its default are unchanged by this experiment.</p></details>''')
(root/'report.html').write_text(''.join(parts))
